# modules/sast/rules/python.rules - docs/DESIGN.md §6.3 "python" seed catalog:
# eval/exec, pickle, yaml.load, subprocess shell=True, os.system, Flask
# debug=True, Jinja autoescape=False.
#
# SAST-PY-YAML_UNSAFE_LOAD-01 closes docs/FOUNDATION.md finding F4: this is
# the SHIPPED equivalent of rules/RULE-FORMAT.md §12.2's worked example, and
# carries `context-window: 0` per F4's frozen direction, not the `2` the old
# (defective) worked example used - a coincidental SafeLoader mention up to
# two lines away must never suppress a genuine, unrelated yaml.load() call.
# See tests/suites/sast.sh "F4 regression" for the test that fails under the
# window-2 reading.

id: SAST-PY-EVAL_EXEC-01
title: Use of eval() or exec() on request-derived data
severity: critical
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-95
owasp: A05:2025
pattern: \b(eval|exec)\s*\(
dialect: ere
files: *.py
tags: static
tags: quick
remediation: Do not pass request-derived data to eval()/exec().
  Parse literals with ast.literal_eval(), or dispatch through an explicit allowlist of
  permitted operations.
references: CWE-95

id: SAST-PY-PICKLE_LOAD-01
title: pickle.load()/loads() on untrusted data
severity: critical
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-502
owasp: A08:2025
pattern: \bpickle\.(load|loads)\s*\(
dialect: ere
files: *.py
tags: static
tags: quick
remediation: Never unpickle data from an untrusted source; pickle can construct arbitrary
  objects and execute arbitrary code during deserialization.
  Use a safe, schema-constrained format such as JSON instead.
references: CWE-502

id: SAST-PY-YAML_UNSAFE_LOAD-01
title: yaml.load() without a safe loader
severity: high
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-502
owasp: A08:2025
pattern: \byaml\.load\s*\(
dialect: ere
files: *.py
files: *.pyi
context-deny: (SafeLoader|CSafeLoader|BaseLoader|yaml\.safe_load)
context-window: 0
tags: static
tags: quick
severity-floor: medium
remediation: Use yaml.safe_load(), or pass Loader=yaml.SafeLoader explicitly on the SAME
  call. yaml.load() with the default loader constructs arbitrary Python objects and is a
  remote code execution sink whenever the document is attacker-influenced.
references: CWE-502

id: SAST-PY-SUBPROCESS_SHELL-01
title: subprocess call with shell=True
severity: high
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-78
owasp: A05:2025
pattern: subprocess\.(call|run|Popen)\([^)]*shell[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*True
dialect: ere
files: *.py
tags: static
remediation: Pass the command as a list with shell=False (the default), so the shell
  never re-interprets metacharacters in an argument.
references: CWE-78

id: SAST-PY-OS_SYSTEM-01
title: os.system() invocation
severity: high
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-78
owasp: A05:2025
pattern: \bos\.system\s*\(
dialect: ere
files: *.py
tags: static
remediation: Replace os.system() with subprocess.run() passing an argument list and
  shell=False, so untrusted input cannot reach a shell.
references: CWE-78

id: SAST-PY-FLASK_DEBUG-01
title: Flask application run or configured with debug enabled
severity: high
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-489
owasp: A02:2025
pattern: (app\.run\([^)]*debug[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*True|app\.debug[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*True)
dialect: ere
files: *.py
tags: static
remediation: Never enable debug mode in production; Flask's debugger exposes an
  interactive Python console reachable by anyone who can trigger an unhandled exception.
references: CWE-489

id: SAST-PY-JINJA_AUTOESCAPE_FALSE-01
title: Jinja2 environment with autoescape disabled
severity: high
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-79
owasp: A05:2025
pattern: autoescape[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*False
dialect: ere
files: *.py
files: *.html
files: *.jinja
files: *.j2
tags: static
remediation: Leave autoescape enabled (or set it True explicitly) so template output is
  HTML-escaped by default; disabling it reintroduces XSS for every variable in the template.
references: CWE-79
